Active disassembly is most promising for high-volume consumer products where manual disassembly is not economically viable — mobile phones, small appliances, IT peripherals, and packaged consumer goods. The technology is also applicable to products containing hazardous materials that benefit from quick, clean separation. The designer must ensure that the activation temperature is well above the product's normal operating range to prevent premature disassembly, and that the smart material elements are compatible with the product's manufacturing processes.